3.3 Generalized Feature Propagation
Given HG, we propose to learn fine-grained news representations by encapsulating the valuable information in entities, topics, and other similar news that share common topics or entities. It is worth noting that we highlight the significance of exploring these high-level semantics not only because of the preliminary results reported in Fig. 2, but also regarding the consensus that fake news carries false knowledge about real entities on a particular topic (Zhou and Zafarani, 2020). Therefore, we take news, entities, and topics into account so as to distinguish the nuances of fake news. We propose to use Generalized PageRank (GPR) for propagating the features of entities, topics, and other news pieces to the target, by simply learning a weighing scalar for each propagation step. To be specific, we first apply a two-layer MLP, fθ(·),
